#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063993 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "94ad8efa-33ee-5451-b6b9-c99cb81a9ba2" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Definite Integrals of Algebraic Functions Using Substitution"}] :question/id #uuid "109a6d6e-8e62-5eac-bfa8-7c059399efe8" :question/math-academy-id "e-457" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_0^{1/2}x(1-2x)^5\\,\\textrm d x$." :question/worked-solution "Let $u=1-2x$. Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = -2\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad -\\dfrac 1 2 \\,\\textrm d u = \\textrm d x\n$$\n\nWe also note that\n\n$$\nx = \\dfrac 1 2 (1-u)\n$$\n\nComputing our limits of integration, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x & 0 & 1/2 \\\\ u & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWe can now solve the integral using our new variable $u$, remembering to use the new limits of integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{0}^{1/2}x(1 - 2x)^{5}dx &= ∫_{1}^{0}\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot (1 - u) \\cdot u^{5} \\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})du \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{4}∫_{1}^{0}(1 - u) \\cdot u^{5}du \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{4}∫_{1}^{0}(u^{5} - u^{6})du \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{4}(\\frac{1}{6}u^{6} - \\frac{1}{7}u^{7}) \\mid _{1}^{0} \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{4}([0 - 0] - [\\frac{1}{6} - \\frac{1}{7}]) \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{4}(-\\frac{1}{42}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{168}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063994 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2feb2115-bd75-5c09-87cc-f10cf46c182f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Indefinite Integrals of Algebraic Functions Using Substitution"}] :question/id #uuid "a40f6e7e-f4d3-5f3e-bf9d-99c640e36274" :question/math-academy-id "e-458" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int x^3\\sqrt{x^2 + 1}\\, \\textrm{d}x$." :question/worked-solution "Let\n\n$$\nu = x^2+1\n$$\n\nThen, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{du}{dx} = 2x⟹\\frac{1}{2}du = xdx\n$$\n\nWe can now solve the integral in terms of $u$, and then express our final answer in terms of $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫x^{3}\\sqrt{x^{2} + 1}dx &= ∫x^{2} \\cdot x\\sqrt{x^{2} + 1}dx \\\\\n&= ∫x^{2}\\sqrt{x^{2} + 1} \\cdot xdx \\\\\n&= ∫x^{2}^(⏞)^(u - 1)\\sqrt{x^{2} + 1} \\cdot xdx^(⏞)^(\\frac{1}{2}du) \\\\\n&= ∫(u - 1)\\sqrt{u} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}du \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}∫(u - 1)u^{1/2}du \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}∫(u^{3/2} - u^{1/2})du \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{2}{5}u^{5/2} - \\frac{2}{3}u^{3/2}) + C \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{5}(x^{2} + 1)^{5/2} - \\frac{1}{3}(x^{2} + 1)^{3/2} + C \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{5}\\sqrt{(x^{2} + 1)^{5}} - \\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt{(x^{2} + 1)^{3}} + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064412 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "94ad8efa-33ee-5451-b6b9-c99cb81a9ba2" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Definite Integrals of Algebraic Functions Using Substitution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bae56b87-940f-5d55-961b-ca0582ee9d8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{32}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061157} {:answer/id #uuid "bed35f76-fe3c-5fd1-8d0b-a88e5eee4284" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{32}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061158} {:answer/id #uuid "c36c7fc9-b108-571e-a645-a80b484e78be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{72}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061159} {:answer/id #uuid "ed33e206-f507-50c8-9fa7-049a11fca55c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{8}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061160} {:answer/id #uuid "4eeb5792-9240-5e4e-8fd0-43a3c7484502" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061161}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed33e206-f507-50c8-9fa7-049a11fca55c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{8}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061160} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ae5a8df-e560-5088-9797-eecb4e87248f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/re